tion between these videos and the  you know the kidnapping of the women or  the disappearance of the women or  whether james's kind of crumbling mental  state is finding patterns and  connections where there aren't any so as  i mentioned earlier uh this is actually  a really intriguing movie it has a great  premise like i said everything is like  all about creepy youtube videos and  conspiracies and [ __ ] like that it has a  really cool like noir sensibility like  even the score is like kind of a jazzy  noir-esque kind of score and like i said  the videos the videos themselves are  like super creepy like i said if you've  seen i feel fantastic like that's creepy  but this is like even creepier than that  but it's along those lines but i do  agree that i mean if you're just  watching this thinking it's gonna be  like a conspiracy and like everything's  gonna be resolved at the end then at the  end you might be like what the [ __ ] just  what the [ __ ] did i just watch and you  might get mad uh because the end is like  kind of abrupt and a lot of stuff is  kind of left unanswered um you're kind  of like well did all this stuff really  happen or was it all in james's  imagination  or something like that and i'm gonna say  i'm inclined to believe the latter that  everything i don't think everything that  happened wasn't james's imagination but  i do think like some of the [ __ ] that  happened was real and some of the people  he talked to were real but the thing  about it is that i think the intention  of the movie and i'm pretty sure that  the intention of the movie was not to be  a conspiracy style mystery uh in that  form it was kind of like i think it's  more exploring how  the sort of like psychological fragility  engendered by grief or uncertainty  can lead a person kind of down these  paths of like unhealthy obsession where  they're starting to look for meaning  where there isn't any so they're finding  like all these meaningless deeds because  there's a lot of  stuff like that like peppered throughout  the film like as he goes along this you  know ride and talks to like all these  various people about what he thinks is  this big conspiracy many people like  kind of warn him off it like people say  things like that like oh you know maybe  nothing means anything or something like  that so i kind of feel like they're  going more into it as  because he doesn't have any closure over  what happened to his wife because she  just disappeared um and he really very  much wants closure so he's trying to  sort of like  find something that will give her  disappearance meaning he wants to find  out what happened to her and he just  really wants everything resolved and  tied up with a bow but life isn't really  like that  now i have seen and this is kind of like  spoiler territory although like i said  you can bring your own theories to it  because i don't think there's i don't  think there's any one particular answer  i think there could be a couple  different theories i'm kind of of the  opinion i thought the first time that i  watched it again spoiler alert spoiler  alert spoiler alert i kind of thought  after i finished watching it that james  had actually killed his wife  and couldn't  deal with it and like dissociated and  then was sort of like constructed most  of this sort of like conspiracy  which most of which was like built  around like real things like but he tied  all the tendrils together like in a way  that maybe absolved him and made it seem  like this bigger conspiracy but it works  either way i kind of feel like it could  be too that because she was found well  she wasn't found like what she  disappeared and all that was found was  her car and it was on a bridge it could  be and i've seen this theory uh kind of  put forth as well that she actually just  committed suicide and he can't really  deal with that either maybe thinking  that he's guilty for like causing her  like driving her to it because of  something that h